**✅ CORRECT: method return type**

```java
// The ONE correct use — "this method might not return a value":
public Optional<Account> findAccount(String accountId) {
    return Optional.ofNullable(accountRepo.findById(accountId));
}

// Caller is FORCED to handle absence:
findAccount("SAV2001")
    .map(Account::getBalance)
    .orElse(BigDecimal.ZERO);
```

**❌ ANTI-PATTERN 1: Optional as a field**

```java
// BAD:
class Customer {
    private Optional<String> middleName;  // ❌ NOT Serializable!
    // JPA won't persist Optional fields
    // Jackson serialization breaks or needs custom config
    // 16 bytes extra allocation per Customer
}

// GOOD:
class Customer {
    private String middleName;  // nullable field — use Optional in getter

    public Optional<String> getMiddleName() {
        return Optional.ofNullable(middleName);  // convert at the BOUNDARY
    }
}
```

**❌ ANTI-PATTERN 2: Optional as a method parameter**

```java
// BAD — forces caller to wrap:
void transferMoney(String from, String to, Optional<BigDecimal> fee) { }
// Caller: transferMoney("A", "B", Optional.of(new BigDecimal("20")));
// Caller: transferMoney("A", "B", Optional.empty());
// What if caller passes null? → NPE on Optional itself!

// GOOD — method overloading or nullable parameter:
void transferMoney(String from, String to) { }                    // no fee
void transferMoney(String from, String to, BigDecimal fee) { }    // with fee
// Or: @Nullable annotation
void transferMoney(String from, String to, @Nullable BigDecimal fee) { }
```

**❌ ANTI-PATTERN 3: Optional in collections**

```java
// BAD:
List<Optional<Trade>> trades;  // ❌ bizarre! Contains empty Optionals?

// GOOD:
List<Trade> trades;  // just exclude null/absent values at source
// If source has nulls: trades.stream().filter(Objects::nonNull).toList()
```

**❌ ANTI-PATTERN 4: .get() without checking**

```java
// BAD — just a different NullPointerException!
Trade trade = findTrade("TRD-999").get();
// NoSuchElementException if empty — same crash, different exception name

// GOOD:
Trade trade = findTrade("TRD-999")
    .orElseThrow(() -> new TradeNotFoundException("TRD-999"));  // clear exception
// Or:
findTrade("TRD-999").ifPresent(this::processTrade);  // safe action
// Or:
Trade trade = findTrade("TRD-999").orElse(defaultTrade);  // safe default
```

